From: Linux3 Build Project <linux3@example.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Force use of -Wl,-Ttext instead of -Wl,--image-base

With binutils 2.46+, -Wl,--image-base,<addr> sets the LOAD segment
base address, but the .text section is placed at <addr> + header_size
(e.g. 0x9000 -> 0x9074). GRUB expects .text to start at exactly the
specified address.

Force the -Wl,-Ttext fallback which correctly places the .text section
at the requested virtual address.

Signed-off-by: Linux3 Build Project <linux3@example.com>

diff -urN a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -40956,7 +40956,7 @@
 if test "x$ax_cv_check_ldflags___Wl___image_base_0x400000" = xyes
 then :
-  TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,--image-base"
+  TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,-Ttext"
 else $as_nop
   TARGET_IMG_BASE_LDOPT="-Wl,-Ttext"
 fi
